iples of design</h3><ul><li><strong>Pattern</strong>: A pattern is a design that repeats. Patterns are found in woven cloth, mats, and borders of pots.</li><li><strong>Balance</strong>: Balance is the even distribution of elements so the design looks stable. Many lowland designs use symmetry, where both sides are the same.</li><li><strong>Rhythm</strong>: Rhythm is the sense of movement created by repeating elements, guiding the eye across the design.</li></ul><h3>Crafts and their origins</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Craft</th><th>Place known for it</th><th>Material</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Inabel weaving</td><td>Ilocos</td><td>Cotton thread</td></tr><tr><td>Burnay jars</td><td>Vigan, Ilocos Sur</td><td>Clay</td></tr><tr><td>Wood carving</td><td>Paete, Laguna</td><td>Wood</td></tr><tr><td>Taka</td><td>Paete, Laguna</td><td>Paper and paste</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Quick check</h3><ol><li>What is burnay and where is it from?</li><li>What is a pattern in design?</li><li>What does symmetry mean in a design?</li></ol><details><summary>Show answers</summary><ol><li>A brown clay jar from Vigan, Ilocos Sur.</li><li>A design that repeats.</li><li>Both sides of the design are the same.</li></ol></details>', 1 FROM courses c
