ns, computer hardware servicing, and creating digital content.</li></ul><h3>Why TLE skills matter</h3><ul><li>They make you more independent and helpful at home.</li><li>They can be used to start a small business.</li><li>They can lead to TESDA certification and employment.</li><li>They develop good work habits like safety, accuracy, and responsibility.</li></ul><h3>TLE areas and sample careers</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Sample skill</th><th>Sample career</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Home Economics</td><td>Cookery</td><td>Cook, caterer</td></tr><tr><td>Industrial Arts</td><td>Electrical installation</td><td>Electrician</td></tr><tr><td>Agri-Fishery Arts</td><td>Crop production</td><td>Farmer, agriculturist</td></tr><tr><td>ICT</td><td>Computer servicing</td><td>Computer technician</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Quick check</h3><ol><li>What does TLE stand for?</li><li>Which TLE area includes carpentry and plumbing?</li><li>Why do Grades 7 and 8 take exploratory courses?</li></ol><details><summary>Show answers</summary><ol><li>Technology and Livelihood Education</li><li>Industrial Arts</li><li>To try different TLE areas before choosing a specialization.</li></ol></details>', 1 FROM courses c
